{c: Chords from the writer's own lead sheet (MusicXML in the source above)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Son comes up. Blood flows [Bm7]down.
Word made [Asus]flesh; Truth made [G]jest; curse made [D]crown.
Sun goes [D]dark. Love's work [Bm7]done.
Landscapes [Asus]shake; strongholds [G]quake; Love has [D]won.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Precious [G]Lord, please for[D]give.
Draw me [G]close; help me [D]live [D/F#]for you.
[A]Precious [D]Lord.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Here I [D]stand, no de[Bm7]fense.
Stained by [Asus]sin, scrubbing [G]crimson finger[D]prints.
Son comes [D]up. Day breaks [Bm7]new.
Life beats [Asus]Death; Christ breathes [G]breath; Love breaks [D]through.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus 2}
Precious [G]Lord, please for[D]give.
Draw me [G]close; help me [D]live [D/F#]for you.
[A]And one [Bm7]day, [G]let my re[D]ward
[D/F#]Be the [A]sight of [G]my Precious [D]Lord.
{end_of_chorus}
